// AWS Root Account API Usage  [tier: alert]  ATT&CK: T1078.004
// Detects any API activity performed by the account root user (outside of console sign-in). Best practice is to never use root for day-to-day…
// False positives: Rare account/billing operations that can only be performed by root.
// Source: rules/initial-access/root-account-api-usage.yml — generated by scripts/build_dist.py; adjust field names to your CloudTrail schema.
userIdentity.type=/^Root$/i not eventName=/^ConsoleLogin$/i
